NAME
    mon - the YACC1 ROM monitor

SYNOPSIS
    exit                 from the Y1/OS shell
    >                    the monitor's prompt

DESCRIPTION
    The monitor in ROM at $F000 is where the YACC1 starts and where
    Y1/OS's exit returns. It reads one-letter commands, upper or lower
    case, at its ">" prompt; an address is four hex digits. After B, D,
    E and F a bare Enter carries on where the command left off.

    The commands (H prints this list):
        0          leave (the emulators only)
        H          the help list
        B AAAA     show 256 bytes from AAAA (16-byte aligned)
        D AAAA     show 16 bytes from AAAA (16-byte aligned)
        E AAAA     show the byte at AAAA as AAAA:XX; two hex digits
                   store a new value, Enter goes to the next byte
        F AAAA     fill 256 bytes from AAAA with 0
        G AAAA     call the program at AAAA (JSRUR R7); it returns
                   with RET
        R          show the registers
        V?         the video card's commands (2026-09-25): VS status,
                   VP probe, VI init the CRTC + clear, VC clear, VM1 /
                   VM0 mirror the console on the screen, VW RR CC TEXT
                   write text at row/column, VB AAAA BB.. store bytes,
                   VF BB fill, VD the screen as text, VR RR [VV] a
                   CRTC register (see video)
        O          boot Y1/OS from the CompactFlash card
        I          BASIC
        L          list the BASIC program
        P          enter a BASIC program line
        C          copy the BASIC test program into the buffer
        Y          run the BASIC test code
        Z          run the program with the BASIC interpreter
        :          Intel-hex load (tools/monload.py sends a .img)

    O prints "BOOT FROM CF", initialises the card, reads the boot block
    (LBA 0), checks its P8 signature and sector count, reads the OS
    from LBA 1 to $1000 and calls it; "CF ERROR" or "NO OS ON THE CARD"
    when that fails.

    The monitor's BIOS vectors ($FFC0..$FFFC: console, CF sectors) and
    its variable page ($0F00: the syscall block, ARGBUF) are what Y1/OS
    and every program build on; see abi.

EXAMPLES
    O               boot Y1/OS
    B 5000          after exit: the program area as the last program
                    left it

NOTES
    BASIC's token buffer ($1000..$1FFF) is where the OS lives: after
    BASIC, boot again with O (which always reloads the OS anyway).
    Removed from the P8X version: mon as a shell command (type exit).
    The page is rewritten for the YACC1 monitor
    (firmware/monitor/monitor.asm) from P8X os/man/mon 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
